                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Constituents are waiting in a holding pattern, uncertain about the future, hoping that Congress will resolve the issue before they purchase their insurance.\u00a0Many respondents indicated that either they or a family member had received specialized medical care. They concluded that alternatives included possibly switching doctors, choosing a different plan, reducing other expenses to maintain their coverage, or forgoing coverage altogether. Some mentioned taking out a home equity line of credit. Others indicated taking on additional employment or delving into 401(k) accounts to accommodate their healthcare needs, realizing that at retirement, their savings would likely be depleted. Another constituent shared that he needed to find money from somewhere because he didn't know where it would come from at this time.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1762382876,
                "view_count": 22
            },
            {
