                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Friday in the First\n\nWilliam \u201cBill\u201d Kearney, a resident of Warrenton, is an associate minister and coordinator of faith and health ministries at Coley Springs Missionary Baptist Church. He has served as faith and health ministry coordinator for the United Shiloh Missionary Baptist Association and as president of the United Shiloh Association Church Union. \n\nRev. Kearney works as a community outreach manager and researcher at the UNC-CH Center for Health Promotion and Disease Prevention and founded and leads the Warren County Environmental Action Team. He aims to improve access to healthy foods, physical activity, and supportive environments. He's part of the Food Fitness Opportunity Research Collaborative at UNC-CH, chairs the Warren County Juvenile Crime Prevention Council, and coordinated Warren County Youth Services Bureau initiatives. He also serves on the Warren County Food Policy Council and Farmers Market Committee. \n\nRev. Kearney has helped develop programs for at-risk youth, facilitated youth research projects, and contributed to a master parks and recreation plan as a member of the Warren County Parks and Recreation Committee. We recognize him for his many roles and for giving back to the community. \n\n#FridaySpotlight",
